KG42.register("source_edge_archive-05fe1b433992ad4599903681",{"id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R002::E::v141-c-R002-E001","paper":"13-consensus_product_differentiation","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","rule_ref":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R002","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R002-E001","source":"coordination.price_signal","target":"bidding.supply","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R002-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R002-C003"],"semantic_review_status":"partial","source":"COMP-fe1c33d7a61b4b97","target":"COMP-b3f649e90c1f17b9","source_occurrence_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R002::V::coordination.price_signal","target_occurrence_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R002::V::bidding.supply","source_unit_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::M01::coordination.price_signal","target_unit_id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::M01::bidding.supply","omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Aggregate producer supply feasibility and RCI treatment of power boundaries. | Information exchanged by producers with their neighboring negotiating agents during RCI. | Producer bilateral supply quantities in MBED and their RCI updates. | Producer quantity updates in the decentralized RCI implementation of MBED. | The direct-solution approach discussed for MBED local subproblems. | Within-iteration ordering of RCI updates for producers.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g01-e32","v141-b-g01-e33","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e19"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"cc5af783f9146d2a5b71fa5e80e736f60e24f7619b75bc0027eda1a4bb7476dd","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"M01","source_definition":"The producer's current offered bilateral quantity enters the price-estimate update through the trading-reciprocity imbalance term. Scope: Producer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. Condition: During an RCI price update involving a producer's bilateral quantity. The consumer's current requested bilateral quantity enters the price-estimate update through the trading-reciprocity imbalance term. Scope: Consumer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. Condition: During an RCI price update involving a consumer's bilateral quantity. Performing the RCI updates requires sharing the producer's current offered bilateral quantity with its communication neighbor as part of the mandatory quantity-and-price message. Scope: Producer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration, for a producer and its communication neighbor. Performing the RCI updates requires sharing the consumer's current requested bilateral quantity with its communication neighbor as part of the mandatory quantity-and-price message. Scope: Consumer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration, for a consumer and its communication neighbor. Each agent must send its bilateral price estimate to its communication neighbor as part of the prescribed information exchange. Scope: Per-iteration communication between neighboring agents in RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration. The participants' separately calculated price estimates for a given bilateral trade must agree, λ_nm = λ_mn. Scope: Individually calculated price estimates for the same bilateral trade in the fully decentralized RCI implementation. Condition: After convergence. Reaching optimality through RCI does not require sharing agents' internal production/consumption parameters or product-differentiation criterion parameters. Scope: Information disclosure in the RCI implementation of MBED. The iterative process stops when convergence is established; convergence criterion (26) is optional. Scope: Termination of iterative RCI coordination. Condition: When algorithmic convergence is established under the prescribed stopping criteria.","target_definition":"Price-signal coordination supplies the perceived-price input to the inverse-gradient target power setpoint used in updating the producer's bilateral offered quantity. Scope: Producer quantity updates in the decentralized RCI implementation of MBED. Condition: Agent n operates as a producer during an RCI iteration. Updating the trading-price dual variables precedes updating the producer's bilateral offered quantities; power-boundary dual updates also occur before the quantity-update step. Scope: Within-iteration ordering of RCI updates for producers. Condition: Each RCI iteration containing the producer P-update. Different price offers lead the producer to try to concentrate its offered quantity with the neighboring agent having the most interesting price and offer nothing to the others; the source describes direct-solution outcomes as usually binary. Scope: The direct-solution approach discussed for MBED local subproblems. Condition: A producer's local subproblem is solved directly with different offered trade prices. Each bilateral offered quantity is constrained to be nonnegative. The producer P-update enforces this sign restriction through its max operator at each iteration. Scope: Producer bilateral supply quantities in MBED and their RCI updates. Condition: Agent n operates as a producer. The sum of a producer's bilateral offered quantities is subject to its lower and upper power-injection bounds. RCI enforces the power-boundary constraints through Lagrangian relaxation. Scope: Aggregate producer supply feasibility and RCI treatment of power boundaries. Condition: Producer quantities must satisfy the bounds at a feasible MBED solution; the RCI implementation treats these constraints through Lagrangian relaxation. A producer must send its current bilateral offered quantity to the corresponding neighboring agent as part of the prescribed quantity-and-price information bundle. Scope: Information exchanged by producers with their neighboring negotiating agents during RCI. Condition: At each RCI iteration.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Price-signal coordination supplies the perceived-price input to the inverse-gradient target power setpoint used in updating the producer's bilateral offered quantity. Scope: Producer quantity updates in the decentralized RCI implementation of MBED. Condition: Agent n operates as a producer during an RCI iteration.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal","bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Different price offers lead the producer to try to concentrate its offered quantity with the neighboring agent having the most interesting price and offer nothing to the others; the source describes direct-solution outcomes as usually binary. Scope: The direct-solution approach discussed for MBED local subproblems. Condition: A producer's local subproblem is solved directly with different offered trade prices.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal","bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e23"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p02-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":2,"printed_page":"995","section":"II-A. Peer-to-Peer Trading","anchor_text":"actual power network (being, e.g., transmission and distribution er grids, or possibly a microgrid),","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"To model this trading scheme, the net power injection P_n of each agent n ∈ Ω is split into a sum of bilaterally traded quantities with a set of neighboring agents m ∈ ω_n, i.e., P_n = Σ_{m∈ω_n} P_nm (1). A positive value corresponds to a sale/production and a negative value to a purchase/consumption. The set {P_nm | n ∈ Ω, m ∈ ω_n} is the set of decision variables. To lighten notations P_n is also used for the whole set of transactions of agent n."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e22","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":"997","section":"III-A. Structure of the Method","anchor_text":"al aims at solving his own local problem while reacting on the he primal and dual estimates of other","equation_id":"(10a), (10b), (10c), (10d)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The local optimization problem of a given agent n ∈ Ω at a given iteration k is min_{D_n} C_n(P_n) + C̃_n(p_n) − p_n^⊤ λ_n^k (10a) s.t. P_n ≤ P_n ≤ P̄_n (10b) P_nm ≥ 0 ∀m ∈ ω_n if n ∈ Ω_p (10c) P_nm ≤ 0 ∀m ∈ ω_n if n ∈ Ω_c (10d) where λ_n^k = (λ_nm^k)_{m∈ω_n} is the vector of price estimates of agent n at iteration k, p_n^⊤ is the transposed vector of p_n and D_n = (p_n ∈ R^{|ω_n|})."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e23","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":"997","section":"III-A. Structure of the Method","anchor_text":"(10d) he m where λkn = (λknm)m∈ωn is the vector of price estimates of ly agent n at iteration k, p⊤n","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In contrast with to the dual ascent method, the local optimization problem is not solved directly as this may affect the solving of the MBED problem. First of all, solving of the local problem can be computationally costly due to the high number of decision variables per agent. A solution can be to replace that complete solving step with a gradient step and a projection on the feasibility set [5], [19]. Additionally, a direct approach to solve local sub-problems in the MBED will most often results in binary outcomes: when offered different prices, an agent will always try to trade as much as possible from the neighboring agent with the most interesting price and nothing from the others."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e28","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":"998","section":"III-C. Primal Updates","anchor_text":"problem at iteration k presented in (10) can be expressed as Llocn (pn, λkn, μn, μn) = Cn(pn) + Cn(p","equation_id":"(16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"For any trade between two agents n and m, we define a new price, referred to as the perceived price, through λ̂_nm = λ_nm − c_nm (16) By opposition, the trading reciprocity constraint dual variables (λ_nm) are referred to as trading prices. As an example, in a tax implementation of product differentiation, the perceived price corresponds to the price after tax, while trading prices correspond to the price before tax."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e14","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p06-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":"999","section":"III-C. Primal Updates","anchor_text":"SORIN et al.: CONSENSUS-BASED APPROACH TO PEER-TO-PEER ELECTRICITY MARK The Lagrangian of the relaxe","equation_id":"(18)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The Lagrangian of the relaxed problem has bijective gradient when seen as function of the power setpoints. For each negoti-ated trade (between agent n and m, a target power setpoint can be deﬁne using the inverse gradient, i.e.,\n              ˆλnm −μn + μn −bn\n                                                         (18)\n                   an                       P n(m),k+1 ="},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e15","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p06-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":"999","section":"III-C. Primal Updates","anchor_text":"SORIN et al.: CONSENSUS-BASED APPROACH TO PEER-TO-PEER ELECTRICITY MARK The Lagrangian of the relaxe","equation_id":"(19)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The primal variables are then updated following (19), referred to as P-update (here for a producer),\n  P nmk+1 = max  0, P nmk + fnmk  P n(m),k+1 −P nk       (19)\n... The max operator in (19) is used to enforce the sign constraint of the decision variables and is replaced in the case of a consumer by a min operator."}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Aggregate producer supply feasibility and RCI treatment of power boundaries. | Information exchanged by producers with their neighboring negotiating agents during RCI. | Producer bilateral supply quantities in MBED and their RCI updates. | Producer quantity updates in the decentralized RCI implementation of MBED. | The direct-solution approach discussed for MBED local subproblems. | Within-iteration ordering of RCI updates for producers.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g01-e32","v141-b-g01-e33","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e19"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R002-E001","source":"coordination.price_signal","target":"bidding.supply","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15"]},"paper_scope_note":"The λ update, P update, and required communication of RCI have direct formula basis; only protocol component dependencies are allowed, and the values of k and k+1 or the roles of consumer and producer are not conflated."}});
